Automates manual CLI testing using stateful, user-journey test flows.

1. Test Execution & Statefulness
- A single sandbox fixture is provisioned per BaseFixtureTest subclass.
- Test methods (assert_*) run sequentially in order of declaration against the same mutating sandbox state.
- Individual assert_* methods can return either a single test spec dictionary or an ordered list of test specs
- Within an assert class, atomic tests are carried out in order mandated by
    - assert method declaration order
    - method internal order of list carried test-spec objects

2. Reporting
   - BaseFixtureTest captures CLI results (exit_code, exit_msg, clipboards, frames_count, missing_fs_paths) for each step.
   - On completion, ship_gate.py flushes a detailed JSON report payload to disk.

3. Feedback & Inspection
   - The GateInspector parses the generated JSON report.
   - Formats and outputs human-readable console feedback summarizing pass/fail status and state mismatches for the developer.